-- Q711: Derivatives and Hedging [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-30-35-3, the effective portion of a cash flow hedge is recorded in OCI, while the ineffective portion -- the amount by which the derivative''s gain or loss exceeds the change in expected cash flows -- must be recognized in current period earnings immediately. This ensures only the risk-offsetting component receives deferred treatment.
Wrong (A): OCI treatment applies to the effective portion, not the ineffective portion; the ineffective amount bypasses OCI entirely.
Wrong (C): Adjusting the hedged item''s carrying amount (basis adjustment) applies when reclassifying from OCI upon settlement, not for recognizing hedge ineffectiveness.
Wrong (D): There is no deferred-and-amortized treatment for hedge ineffectiveness; ASC 815 requires immediate earnings recognition.$EXPL$
