-- Q714: Derivatives and Hedging [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-35-35-1, the effective portion of a net investment hedge gain or loss is recognized in the cumulative translation adjustment (CTA) within other comprehensive income. This mirrors the translation adjustment on the foreign subsidiary''s net assets, creating a consistent offset within the same OCI component. CTA amounts remain in accumulated OCI until the subsidiary is sold or substantially liquidated.
Wrong (A): Recognizing the gain in current period earnings would defeat the purpose of net investment hedge accounting, which defers recognition in the CTA.
Wrong (C): Retained earnings is not a valid destination for hedging gains; the CTA within OCI is required under ASC 815.
Wrong (D): Cost of goods sold relates to inventory transactions, not to hedging gains on a net investment in a foreign operation.$EXPL$
