-- Q716: Derivatives and Hedging [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 815, a call option grants the holder the right -- but not the obligation -- to purchase the underlying asset at the strike price. Crestline exercises at $5.50 when the market is $6.10, yielding a gross payoff of ($6.10 - $5.50) x 10,000 = $6,000. After deducting the $3,200 premium, the net gain is $2,800.
Wrong (A): A call option is the right to buy, not the right to sell; that describes a put option.
Wrong (B): Options grant rights, not obligations; an obligation to transact describes a forward or futures contract, and net gain must reflect the premium paid.
Wrong (D): The strike price is $5.50, not $6.10; using the market price as the exercise price misunderstands strike price mechanics.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 716;

